WEBVTT

00:00:06.283 --> 00:00:07.004
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.494
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> This beautiful elephant is an example of Dhokra metal art,

00:00:14.056 --> 00:00:19.163
which originated in India over four thousand years ago.

00:00:20.064 --> 00:00:26.361
The technique involves carving a figure out of wax, covering this with clay,

00:00:26.671 --> 00:00:34.027
baking the clay until the wax melts, and then filling the hollow clay with liquid metal.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:36.871
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:37.952 --> 00:00:45.820
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Archaeologists have discovered over a hundred thousand different pieces of ancient Greek pottery,

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.631
all of which date back to the first millennium B.C.

00:00:51.802 --> 00:00:57.027
Much of it was produced locally for everyday and kitchen use,

00:00:57.719 --> 00:01:02.166
but the finer pieces were intended purely for decoration.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:04.982
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:01:06.084 --> 00:01:09.680
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> This necklace, known as a broad collar,

00:01:10.135 --> 00:01:14.251
would probably have been worn by an Egyptian pharaoh,

00:01:14.677 --> 00:01:21.272
or placed around the neck of a statue. Broad collars were made of metal,

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:30.020
and typically consisted of rows of beads, made out of gold, glass, or gemstones.

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:32.870
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:01:33.996 --> 00:01:42.381
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> This helmet, or galea, is typical of the ones worn by soldiers of the Roman Empire.

00:01:43.392 --> 00:01:48.406
It has a bowl to protect the skull, a large neck guard,

00:01:48.887 --> 00:01:55.162
a band to protect the forehead, and cheek plates to protect the face.